  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0130\" consists of 8 tables.\nThe \"badges\" table is used to store information about user badges. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), UserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), Name (a string), and Date (a datetime).\nThe \"comments\" table is used to store information about user comments. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), PostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), Score (an integer), Text (a long text), CreationDate (a datetime), UserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), and UserDisplayName (a string).\nThe \"postHistory\" table is used to store information about post history. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), PostHistoryTypeId (an integer), PostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), RevisionGUID (a string), CreationDate (a datetime), UserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), Text (a long text), Comment (a text), and UserDisplayName (a string).\nThe \"postLinks\" table is used to store information about post links. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), CreationDate (a datetime), PostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), RelatedPostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), and LinkTypeId (an integer).\nThe \"posts\" table is used to store information about posts. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), PostTypeId (an integer), AcceptedAnswerId (an integer), CreationDate (a datetime), Score (an integer), ViewCount (an integer), Body (a long text), OwnerUserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), LastActivityDate (a datetime), Title (a string), Tags (a string), AnswerCount (an integer), CommentCount (an integer), FavoriteCount (an integer), LastEditorUserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), LastEditDate (a datetime), CommunityOwnedDate (a datetime), ParentId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), ClosedDate (a datetime), OwnerDisplayName (a string), and LastEditorDisplayName (a string).\nThe \"tags\" table is used to store information about tags. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), TagName (a string), Count (an integer), ExcerptPostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), and WikiPostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table).\nThe \"users\" table is used to store information about users. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), Reputation (an integer), CreationDate (a datetime), DisplayName (a string), LastAccessDate (a datetime), WebsiteUrl (a string), Location (a string), AboutMe (a long text), Views (an integer), UpVotes (an integer), DownVotes (an integer), AccountId (an integer), Age (an integer), and ProfileImageUrl (a string).\nFinally, the \"votes\" table is used to store information about votes. It includes columns for Id (an integer, primary key), PostId (an integer, foreign key referencing the posts table), VoteTypeId (an integer), CreationDate (a date), UserId (an integer, foreign key referencing the users table), and BountyAmount (an integer). All foreign keys have on delete cascade on update cascade rules, meaning that if a record in the parent table is deleted or updated, the corresponding records in the child table will automatically be deleted or updated.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a data management system for the Stats Stack Exchange network. The system captures and stores anonymized user-contributed content, facilitating the analysis and tracking of user interactions and contributions within the network.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to create a robust database that organizes and maintains structured data on user activities, posts, comments, and interactions. This supports data analysis and insights generation for community management and improvement.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Site Administrators: Manage the database and ensure data integrity.\n- Data Analysts: Use the data for insights and reporting.\n- Community Managers: Monitor user interactions and engagement.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. User Management: Maintain user profiles, including reputation, display name, and activity metrics.\n2. Post Management: Track posts, including creation dates, scores, view counts, and relationships with other posts.\n3. Comment Management: Record comments with associated metadata like scores, creation dates, and user information.\n4. Badge Management: Log badge awards to users, documenting achievement types and award dates.\n5. Vote Management: Capture votes on posts, detailing the type of vote and any associated bounty amounts.\n6. Tagging System: Organize content using tags; maintain information about tags and their associated posts.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a large volume of data with efficient query performance.\n- Data Integrity: Ensure consistency and accuracy of data, with cascade update and delete operations across related tables.\n- Anonymity: Maintain user anonymity while preserving engagement metrics.\n- Security: Protect sensitive data and limit access to authorized personnel only.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0130.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0130\nCREATE TABLE `badges` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `badges_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `text` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `postHistory` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_history_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `revision_guid` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `text` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `postHistory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `postHistory_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `postLinks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `related_post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `link_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `postLinks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `postLinks_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`related_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `posts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `accepted_answer_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `view_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `owner_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_activity_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `answer_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `favorite_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_editor_user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_edit_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `community_owned_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `closed_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_editor_display_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`last_editor_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`accepted_answer_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `excerpt_post_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `wiki_post_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`excerpt_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`wiki_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reputation` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_access_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `about_me` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `views` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `up_votes` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `down_votes` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bounty_amount` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
